# realifyAi — environment configuration.
# Copy to ".env" (same folder as package.json):  cp .env.example .env
# Vite auto-loads any VITE_* variable from .env into import.meta.env — no
# other wiring needed; just restart `npm run dev` after changing this file.

# ---- Backend origin ----
# Leave this UNSET for everyday local dev: vite.config.js already proxies
# every /api/* request to http://localhost:8001, so `npm run dev` next to
# `python run.py serve` (in realify-mc) just works with no .env at all.
#
# Set VITE_BACKEND_URL when the backend is NOT on localhost:8001 — an
# ngrok/tunnel URL, a staging deploy, teammate's machine, etc. Once set,
# requests go straight to that origin instead of through the dev proxy, so
# the backend's CORS allowlist (realify-mc/.env's APP_URL) must include
# this frontend's own origin (e.g. http://localhost:5173) for login/session
# cookies to work.
# VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://your-ngrok-subdomain.ngrok-free.app
